  "description": "Version-24 64-episode State College NMCC-PI pilot for 2,500 individual evacuees, same physical scenario as v23. At every training decision the simulator is snapshotted and every feasible cell (first two decisions) or six cells (later) is installed and continued to the horizon with the route-saving base policy under one shared independent noise tape; the actor fits the KL-constrained MPO target q ~ pi_old exp(A/eta) by cross-entropy (epsilon 0.5, eta floor 0.03, trust-region cap 0.6 on KL(pi_new || pi_old) with a parameter-space line search to the boundary, up to 32 epochs). The actor prior is the route-time-saving feature. The intervention-value ensemble is trained on within-state contrasts and scored on held-out rollouts; model fill-in stays off in this pilot. The observation encoder and episode LSTM are shared: the critic, value and intervention-value losses also train them, under an exact policy-preservation term KL(pi_ref || pi) with a 0.05-nat transactional cap. The legacy hybrid NMCC branches, guidance, teacher and staged phases are off.",
